From 71315209e04eb2432f88999e93ace71d8cb89431 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: S10 mainline recon <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 19:44:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: samsung: exynos9820: add the CMU_DPU and CMU_CMGP blocks

CMU_DPU gates the DECON, the DMA of the DPP channels, the APB bus of DSIM0
and the three display System MMUs.  CMU_CMGP gates the I2C controller the
display PMIC hangs off.  Without them the whole display path has no clock
provider, so decon0, dsim0, the three sysmmu nodes and i2c@15d50000 never
probe.

Base addresses, mux and divider layout, gate offsets, field widths and the
parent of every gate are transcribed from the vendor clock abstraction
layer tables (drivers/soc/samsung/cal-if/exynos9820/cmucal-sfr.c and
cmucal-node.c of LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_exynos9820 at
7d08ec364a06).

The clock identifiers the two blocks need are added to
include/dt-bindings/clock/exynos9820.h in the same patch, otherwise the
driver does not build.

Not verified on hardware: the gate offsets and the split between
CLK_IS_CRITICAL and ordinary gates are transcribed, not measured, and the
gating bit 21 is carried over from a single documented example to all 28
gates.  The first parent of both CMU_CMGP muxes is an RCO whose frequency
no available source documents, and it is modelled as the 26 MHz oscillator.

Signed-off-by: S10 mainline recon <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos9820.c   | 263 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/dt-bindings/clock/exynos9820.h |  40 ++++
 2 files changed, 303 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos9820.c b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos9820.c
index cb2aa75..a678bd1 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos9820.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos9820.c
@@ -1512,6 +1512,263 @@ static const struct samsung_cmu_info apm_cmu_info __initconst = {
 	.clk_name		= "bus",
 };
 
+/*
+ * Register offsets for CMU_CMGP (0x15c00000)
+ */
